<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Atholl</h1><p class="st-meta">600 CE – 900 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Pictish kingdom in the central Highlands whose name, 'New Ireland', hints at Gaelic influence, later a Scottish earldom.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atholl">Atholl</a>, Athfotla, appears in Irish annals from the 8th century, when a king of Atholl was drowned by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oengus-i-of-the-picts">Oengus son of Fergus</a>, king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/picts">Picts</a>, in 739. The name is usually interpreted as 'New Ireland', suggesting Gaelic settlement or influence in the Pictish highlands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/perthshire">Perthshire</a>. Fotla is also one of the seven Pictish provinces.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atholl">Atholl</a> seems to have had its own kings within the Pictish overkingship. Its lands in the valleys of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-tay">Tay</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-tummel">Tummel</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-garry-perthshire">Garry</a> were pastoral and thinly peopled. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dunkeld">Dunkeld</a>, on its edge, became a major church centre in the 9th century.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atholl">Atholl</a> was absorbed into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-scotland">Kingdom of Scotland</a> as a mormaerdom and later an earldom. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crinan-of-dunkeld">Crinan</a>, abbot of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dunkeld">Dunkeld</a> and father of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duncan-i-of-scotland">Duncan I</a>, is sometimes linked with Atholl, and its later earls descended from Duncan's family.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 600 CE – 900 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">British Isles</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:71.64%;width:5.97%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>600 CE – 900 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Talorcan mac Drostan</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Pictish; Gaelic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-kingdom">United Kingdom</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Fotla, Athfotla</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=750&amp;focus=kingdom-of-atholl" aria-label="Kingdom of Atholl on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4639 288 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Atholl lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4892 500h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4959 544h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M4959 544h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day United Kingdom. <a href="/atlas?year=750&amp;focus=kingdom-of-atholl">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
